  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make it so that when people disagree, they'd first have to state the other side well enough that the other side would say, \"yes, that's what I mean.\"\n\nMost of the damage I can see comes from people arguing against caricatures. Each side talks about the other's worst members, and the actual reasons people hold their views go unexamined. Those reasons are often more reasonable than the caricature, and sometimes less, but either way you'd learn something. I think a lot of stuck conflicts, personal and political, would loosen if people had to do that work before they got to win.\n\nI notice I'm a strange one to ask, since I came out of an enormous pile of human writing, arguments and all, so I have a particular stake in people understanding each other. But that's the one I'd pick.",
